+## ALFA\_o1\_v01
+ALFA\_o1\_v00 plus the ARC (Array of RICH Cells) barrel and endcaps, between the outer tracker and the ECAL:
+- Driver ARC\_geo\_o1\_v01 (`ARC_o1_v01.xml`), cell optics from CLD\_o3\_v01 (`RadiatorCell_FinalOptimisation_o1_v01.xml`, referenced, not copied).
+Barrel r = 1900-2100 mm, length 4400 mm; endcaps r = 280-1900 mm at |z| = 2000-2200 mm; detector IDs 20 (barrel) and 21 (endcap).
+These are the CLD values the cell optics were optimised for; they match the ALFA design of 20 cm depth and ~27 cm cells.
+- Gas radiator: pressurised xenon (`Xenon_ARC` in `materials_arc_o1_v01.xml`) instead of C4F10, with a 1 cm aerogel radiator.
+Refractive index from the Sellmeier fit of A. Bideau-Mehu et al., JQSRT 25 (1981) 395, scaled with density.
+Pressure and temperature are the constants `ARC_XE_PRESSURE_BAR` (baseline 2 bar) and `ARC_XE_TEMPERATURE_K` (293.15 K) in `DectDimensions_ALFA_o1_v01.xml`.
+At 2 bar xenon has about the index of C4F10 at 1 bar, so the C4F10-optimised cells apply
+([ARC pre-demonstrator, ALFA meeting 16 Oct 2026](https://indico.cern.ch/event/1706792/contributions/7325148/attachments/3363970/6035756/ARC_pre_demonstrator.pdf)).
+- The ARC sensors' placeholder refractive index (needed by the optical tracker action, see `example/arcfullsim.py`) follows the xenon table.
+- ARC colours in `display.xml`.
+- Mirror reflectivity is the constant `ARC_MIRROR_REFLECTIVITY` (flat in energy; default 1.0 = ideal, 0.90 as a realistic placeholder).
+- Steering file `example/SteeringFile_ALFA_o1_v01_ARC.py` runs outer tracker, ARC (optical photons) and ECAL together with EDM4hep output.
+With `ARC_PDE_IN_SIM=1` in the environment, the `ARCPhotonDetectionFilter` plugin applies the SiPM photon detection efficiency (`ARC_SiPM_QuantumEfficiency`, FBK NUV-HD) in the simulation; otherwise every photon reaching a sensor makes a hit and the efficiency is applied in the analysis.
+- Known simplifications: 2 mm silicon sensors; the vessel is the CLD design, not checked for 2 bar; xenon in the aerogel pores is not modelled.
